log\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-05-06\",\n    \"community_feedback\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n    \"title\": \"Copilot Code Review Billing Changes (Effective June 1, 2026)\",\n    \"description\": \"GitHub announced changes to Copilot code review billing where each review will be billed as AI usage and start consuming GitHub Actions minutes.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"announcement\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-05-15\",\n    \"community_feedback\": [\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"Seems like a strong signal the money burning party is coming to a close. Nearly all AI companies have tightened their belts in the past month.\",\n        \"source\": \"HN\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"This was my first thought too. 'The Porsche you rented at $200/mo is now a Honda. But the price hasn't changed!'\",\n        \"source\": \"HN\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"Plan prices aren't changing - just the value you get from those plans has plummeted. It's classic deceptive sales language.\",\n        \"source\": \"HN\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"27x multiplier on Opus is the tell. That is not a pricing model designed for broad adoption, it's a price signal that says 'use the cheaper model.'\",\n        \"source\": \"HN\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"I will not be renewing/switching over, either. I had copilot mainly so I could write issues and throw agents at it.\",\n        \"source\": \"HN\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"Enterprise gets pooled credits and will like having everything go through one place so I think it still works.\",\n        \"source\": \"HN\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"productName\": \"Gemini CLI\",\n   